IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa7-ch3d.l4: Part 13 Chapter 3, Resolutions at meetings: proxies, adjourned meetings, electronic communications and
-- class meetings (ss 324 to 335), lines 4150-4278 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Tag conventions are those of coa7-ch1.l4.

§§ `Proxies`

-- ---- s 324 Rights to appoint proxies ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4152 | (1) A member of a company is entitled to appoint another person as his proxy to exercise all or any of his rights to attend and to speak and vote at a meeting of the company.
@ref s 324(1) Rights to appoint proxies (src:4152)
GIVEN `the person appointed is a person other than the member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 324(1) the member is entitled to appoint the person as his proxy` MEANS
    IF `the person appointed is a person other than the member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A member of a company is entitled to appoint another person as his proxy"

-- src:4153 | (2) In the case of a company having a share capital, a member may appoint more than one proxy in relation to a meeting, provided that each proxy is appointed to exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares held by him, or (as the case may be) to a different £10, or multiple of £10, of stock held by him.
@ref s 324(2) Rights to appoint proxies: more than one proxy (src:4153)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each proxy is appointed to exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares held by the member (or a different £10, or multiple of £10, of stock)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 324(2) the member may appoint more than one proxy in relation to the meeting` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company has a share capital`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company having a share capital"
    ELSE IF `each proxy is appointed to exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares held by the member (or a different £10, or multiple of £10, of stock)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a member may appoint more than one proxy in relation to a meeting, provided that each proxy is appointed to exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares held by him" -- MARGINAL a

-- ---- s 324A Obligation of proxy to vote in accordance with instructions -----------------------------------

-- src:4155 | A proxy must vote in accordance with any instructions given by the member by whom the proxy is appointed.
@ref s 324A Obligation of proxy to vote in accordance with instructions (src:4155)
GIVEN `the member gave the proxy instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proxy voted in accordance with those instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 324A the proxy has complied with the instructions given by the member` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the member gave the proxy instructions`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any instructions given by the member by whom the proxy is appointed"
    ELSE IF `the proxy voted in accordance with those instructions`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A proxy must vote in accordance with any instructions given by the member by whom the proxy is appointed" -- FORK F5

-- ---- s 325 Notice of meeting to contain statement of rights ------------------------------------------------

-- src:4157 | (1) In every notice calling a meeting of a company there must appear, with reasonable prominence, a statement informing the member of—
-- src:4158 | (a) his rights under section 324, and
-- src:4159 | (b) any more extensive rights conferred by the company's articles to appoint more than one proxy.
@ref s 325(1) Notice of meeting to contain statement of rights (src:4157-4159)
GIVEN `the notice appears with reasonable prominence in every notice calling the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement informs the member of his rights under section 324` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles confer more extensive rights to appoint more than one proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement informs the member of those more extensive rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 325(1) the notice contains the statement this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice appears with reasonable prominence in every notice calling the meeting`
        AND `the statement informs the member of his rights under section 324`
        AND ((NOT `the articles confer more extensive rights to appoint more than one proxy`) OR `the statement informs the member of those more extensive rights`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In every notice calling a meeting of a company there must appear, with reasonable prominence, a statement informing the member of— (a) his rights under section 324, and (b) any more extensive rights conferred by the company's articles to appoint more than one proxy" -- FORK F5

-- src:4160 | (2) Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of the meeting or of anything done at the meeting.
@ref s 325(2) Notice of meeting to contain statement of rights: validity (src:4160)
GIVEN `the company failed to comply with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 325(2) the failure affects the validity of the meeting or of anything done at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company failed to comply with this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of the meeting or of anything done at the meeting."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a failure to comply
-- src:4161 | (3) If this section is not complied with as respects any meeting, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 325(3) Notice of meeting to contain statement of rights: offence (src:4161)
GIVEN `this section is not complied with as respects the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 325(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `this section is not complied with as respects the meeting`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If this section is not complied with as respects any meeting, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default." -- MARGINAL a
-- src:4162 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 325(4) Notice of meeting to contain statement of rights: penalty (src:4162)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 325(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is liable on summary conviction"
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- ---- s 326 Company-sponsored invitations to appoint proxies -----------------------------------------------

-- src:4166 | (a) there is issued to a member at his request a form of appointment naming the proxy or a list of persons willing to act as proxy, and
-- src:4167 | (b) the form or list is available on request to all members entitled to vote at the meeting.
@ref s 326(2) Company-sponsored invitations to appoint proxies: not contravened (src:4166-4167)
GIVEN `a form of appointment naming the proxy, or a list of persons willing to act as proxy, is issued to a member at his request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form or list is available on request to all members entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 326(2) subsection (1) is not contravened` MEANS
    IF `a form of appointment naming the proxy, or a list of persons willing to act as proxy, is issued to a member at his request`
        AND `the form or list is available on request to all members entitled to vote at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a safe harbour that fails does not say subsection (1) is contravened -- FORK F10

-- src:4164 | (1) If for the purposes of a meeting there are issued at the company's expense invitations to members to appoint as proxy a specified person or a number of specified persons, the invitations must be issued to all members entitled to vote at the meeting.
@ref s 326(1) Company-sponsored invitations to appoint proxies (src:4164)
GIVEN `invitations are issued at the company's expense to appoint as proxy a specified person or a number of specified persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the invitations are issued to all members entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 326(2) subsection (1) is not contravened` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 326(1) the invitations contravene this subsection` MEANS
    IF (NOT `invitations are issued at the company's expense to appoint as proxy a specified person or a number of specified persons`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If for the purposes of a meeting there are issued at the company's expense invitations to members to appoint as proxy a specified person or a number of specified persons"
    ELSE IF `the invitations are issued to all members entitled to vote at the meeting`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the invitations must be issued to all members entitled to vote at the meeting" -- FORK F5
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 326(2) subsection (1) is not contravened`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) is not contravened if (a) ... and (b) ..."
              OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:4168 | (3) If subsection (1) is contravened as respects a meeting, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 326(3) Company-sponsored invitations to appoint proxies: offence (src:4168)
GIVEN `subsection (1) is contravened as respects the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 326(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `subsection (1) is contravened as respects the meeting`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If subsection (1) is contravened as respects a meeting, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default." -- MARGINAL a
-- src:4169 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 326(4) Company-sponsored invitations to appoint proxies: penalty (src:4169)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 326(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is liable on summary conviction"
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- ---- s 327 Notice required of appointment of proxy etc ---------------------------------------------------

-- src:4172 | (a) the appointment of a person as proxy for a member must be notified to the company in writing;
@ref s 327(A1)(a) Notice required of appointment of proxy etc: notification in writing (src:4172)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment of the person as proxy is notified to the company in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 327(A1)(a) the appointment of the proxy has been notified as this paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a traded company"
    ELSE IF `the appointment of the person as proxy is notified to the company in writing`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the appointment of a person as proxy for a member must be notified to the company in writing" -- FORK F5

DECLARE `s 327(A1)(b) evidence asked for` IS ONE OF
    `s 327(A1)(b)(i) the identity of the member and of the proxy`
    `s 327(A1)(b)(ii) the member's instructions (if any) as to how the proxy is to vote`
    `s 327(A1)(b)(iii) where the proxy is appointed by a person acting on behalf of the member, the authority of that person to make the appointment`
    `s 327(A1)(b) anything else relating to the appointment`

-- src:4173 | (b) where such an appointment is made, the company may require reasonable evidence of—
-- src:4174 | (i) the identity of the member and of the proxy,
-- src:4175 | (ii) the member's instructions (if any) as to how the proxy is to vote, and
-- src:4176 | (iii) where the proxy is appointed by a person acting on behalf of the member, authority of that person to make the appointment;
-- src:4177 | but may not require to be provided with anything else relating to the appointment.
@ref s 327(A1)(b) Notice required of appointment of proxy etc: reasonable evidence (src:4173-4177)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      evidence IS A `s 327(A1)(b) evidence asked for`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 327(A1)(b) the company may require the evidence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`) OR (NOT `the appointment is made`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a traded company ... where such an appointment is made, the company may require reasonable evidence of"
    ELSE CONSIDER evidence
         WHEN `s 327(A1)(b) anything else relating to the appointment` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but may not require to be provided with anything else relating to the appointment"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 327(1) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 327(1)(a) the appointment of a proxy`
    `s 327(1)(b) any document necessary to show the validity of, or otherwise relating to, the appointment of a proxy`
    `s 327(1) another matter`

-- src:4178 | (1) The following provisions apply in the case of traded companies and other companies as regards—
-- src:4179 | (a) the appointment of a proxy, and
-- src:4180 | (b) any document necessary to show the validity of, or otherwise relating to, the appointment of a proxy.
@ref s 327(1) Notice required of appointment of proxy etc: traded companies and other companies (src:4178-4180)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 327(1) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 327(1) the following provisions apply in the case of traded companies and other companies as regards the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 327(1) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as regards— (a) the appointment of a proxy, and (b) any document necessary to show the validity of, or otherwise relating to, the appointment of a proxy"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 327(2) when the document must be received` IS ONE OF
    `s 327(2)(a) in the case of a meeting or adjourned meeting, 48 hours before the time for holding it`
    `s 327(2)(b) in the case of a poll taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded, 24 hours before the time appointed for the taking of the poll`
    `s 327(2) another case`

-- src:4185 | (3) In calculating the periods mentioned in subsection (2) no account shall be taken of any part of a day that is not a working day.
@ref s 327(3) Notice required of appointment of proxy etc: calculating the periods (src:4185)
GIVEN `hours in the period` IS A NUMBER
      `hours of the period that fall on a day that is not a working day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 327(3) the hours of the period that are counted` MEANS
    `hours in the period` MINUS `hours of the period that fall on a day that is not a working day`

-- src:4181 | (2) Any provision of the company's articles is void in so far as it would have the effect of requiring any such appointment or document to be received by the company or another person earlier than the following time—
-- src:4182 | (a) in the case of a meeting or adjourned meeting, 48 hours before the time for holding the meeting or adjourned meeting;
-- src:4183 | (b) in the case of a poll taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded, 24 hours before the time appointed for the taking of the poll;
-- src:4184 | (c) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 327(2) Notice required of appointment of proxy etc: the latest time the articles may require (src:4181-4184)
GIVEN case IS A `s 327(2) when the document must be received`
      `hours before the relevant time that the articles require the appointment or document to be received` IS A NUMBER
      `of those hours, the hours that fall on a day that is not a working day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 327(2) the provision of the articles is void` MEANS
    CONSIDER case
    WHEN `s 327(2) another case` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "earlier than the following time— (a) ... (b) ..."
    WHEN `s 327(2)(a) in the case of a meeting or adjourned meeting, 48 hours before the time for holding it` THEN
        IF `s 327(3) the hours of the period that are counted` `hours before the relevant time that the articles require the appointment or document to be received` `of those hours, the hours that fall on a day that is not a working day` GREATER THAN 48
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is void in so far as it would have the effect of requiring any such appointment or document to be received by the company or another person earlier than the following time"
    WHEN `s 327(2)(b) in the case of a poll taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded, 24 hours before the time appointed for the taking of the poll` THEN
        IF `s 327(3) the hours of the period that are counted` `hours before the relevant time that the articles require the appointment or document to be received` `of those hours, the hours that fall on a day that is not a working day` GREATER THAN 24
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is void in so far as it would have the effect of requiring any such appointment or document to be received by the company or another person earlier than the following time"

-- ---- s 328 Chairing meetings -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4187 | (1) A proxy may be elected to be the chairman of a general meeting by a resolution of the company passed at the meeting.
-- src:4188 | (2) Subsection (1) is subject to any provision of the company's articles that states who may or who may not be chairman.
@ref s 328 Chairing meetings (src:4187-4188)
GIVEN `the person is a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is elected chairman of the general meeting by a resolution of the company passed at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles state who may or who may not be chairman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 328(1) the proxy may be elected chairman of the general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company's articles state who may or who may not be chairman`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subsection (1) is subject to any provision of the company's articles that states who may or who may not be chairman"
    ELSE IF `the person is a proxy` AND `the person is elected chairman of the general meeting by a resolution of the company passed at the meeting`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A proxy may be elected to be the chairman of a general meeting by a resolution of the company passed at the meeting"

-- ---- s 329 Right of proxy to demand a poll ---------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4190 | (1) The appointment of a proxy to vote on a matter at a meeting of a company authorises the proxy to demand, or join in demanding, a poll on that matter.
@ref s 329(1) Right of proxy to demand a poll (src:4190)
GIVEN `the person is appointed as proxy to vote on the matter at a meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 329(1) the proxy is authorised to demand, or join in demanding, a poll on the matter` MEANS
    IF `the person is appointed as proxy to vote on the matter at a meeting of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The appointment of a proxy to vote on a matter at a meeting of a company authorises the proxy to demand, or join in demanding, a poll on that matter"

DECLARE `s 329(2) paragraph of section 321(2)` IS ONE OF
    `s 329(2)(a) paragraph (a) of section 321(2)`
    `s 329(2)(b) paragraph (b) of section 321(2)`
    `s 329(2)(c) paragraph (c) of section 321(2)`

DECLARE `s 329(2) the demand by the proxy counts as` IS ONE OF
    `s 329(2)(a) a demand by the member`
    `s 329(2)(b) a demand by a member representing the voting rights that the proxy is authorised to exercise`
    `s 329(2)(c) a demand by a member holding the shares to which those rights are attached`

-- src:4191 | (2) In applying the provisions of section 321(2) (requirements for effective demand), a demand by a proxy counts—
-- src:4192 | (a) for the purposes of paragraph (a), as a demand by the member;
-- src:4193 | (b) for the purposes of paragraph (b), as a demand by a member representing the voting rights that the proxy is authorised to exercise;
-- src:4194 | (c) for the purposes of paragraph (c), as a demand by a member holding the shares to which those rights are attached.
@ref s 329(2) Right of proxy to demand a poll: how the demand counts (src:4191-4194)
GIVEN `the demand is made by a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      paragraph IS A `s 329(2) paragraph of section 321(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 329(2) the demand by the proxy counts as`
`s 329(2) the demand by the proxy counts` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the demand is made by a proxy`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a demand by a proxy counts"
    ELSE CONSIDER paragraph
         WHEN `s 329(2)(a) paragraph (a) of section 321(2)` THEN JUST `s 329(2)(a) a demand by the member`
         WHEN `s 329(2)(b) paragraph (b) of section 321(2)` THEN JUST `s 329(2)(b) a demand by a member representing the voting rights that the proxy is authorised to exercise`
         WHEN `s 329(2)(c) paragraph (c) of section 321(2)` THEN JUST `s 329(2)(c) a demand by a member holding the shares to which those rights are attached`

-- ---- s 330 Notice required of termination of proxy's authority --------------------------------------------

-- src:4196 | (A1) In the case of a traded company the termination of the authority of a person to act as proxy must be notified to the company in writing.
@ref s 330(A1) Notice required of termination of proxy's authority: traded companies (src:4196)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the termination of the authority of the person to act as proxy is notified to the company in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(A1) the termination has been notified as this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a traded company"
    ELSE IF `the termination of the authority of the person to act as proxy is notified to the company in writing`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the termination of the authority of a person to act as proxy must be notified to the company in writing" -- FORK F5

-- src:4197 | (1) The following provisions apply in the case of traded companies and other companies as regards notice that the authority of a person to act as proxy is terminated (“notice of termination”).
@ref s 330(1) Notice required of termination of proxy's authority: traded companies and other companies (src:4197)
GIVEN `the matter is notice that the authority of a person to act as proxy is terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(1) the following provisions apply in the case of traded companies and other companies as regards the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter is notice that the authority of a person to act as proxy is terminated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as regards notice that the authority of a person to act as proxy is terminated"

DECLARE `s 330(2) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 330(2)(a) whether he counts in deciding whether there is a quorum at a meeting`
    `s 330(2)(b) the validity of anything he does as chairman of a meeting`
    `s 330(2)(c) the validity of a poll demanded by him at a meeting`

-- TRUE says the termination does not affect the matter; FALSE says the bar is lifted (the company received notice of the
-- termination before the commencement of the meeting).
-- src:4198 | (2) The termination of the authority of a person to act as proxy does not affect—
-- src:4199 | (a) whether he counts in deciding whether there is a quorum at a meeting,
-- src:4200 | (b) the validity of anything he does as chairman of a meeting, or
-- src:4201 | (c) the validity of a poll demanded by him at a meeting,
-- src:4202 | unless the company receives notice of the termination before the commencement of the meeting.
@ref s 330(2) Notice required of termination of proxy's authority: quorum, chairman, poll (src:4198-4202)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 330(2) matter`
      `the company receives notice of the termination before the commencement of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(2) the termination of the authority of the person to act as proxy does not affect the matter` MEANS
    IF `the company receives notice of the termination before the commencement of the meeting`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect— (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ..., unless the company receives notice of the termination before the commencement of the meeting" -- FORK F8
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4203 | (3) The termination of the authority of a person to act as proxy does not affect the validity of a vote given by that person unless the company receives notice of the termination—
-- src:4204 | (a) before the commencement of the meeting or adjourned meeting at which the vote is given, or
-- src:4205 | (b) in the case of a poll taken more than 48 hours after it is demanded, before the time appointed for taking the poll.
@ref s 330(3) Notice required of termination of proxy's authority: validity of a vote (src:4203-4205)
GIVEN `the company receives notice of the termination before the commencement of the meeting or adjourned meeting at which the vote is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vote is given on a poll taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company receives notice of the termination before the time appointed for taking the poll` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(3) the termination of the authority of the person to act as proxy does not affect the validity of the vote` MEANS
    IF `the company receives notice of the termination before the commencement of the meeting or adjourned meeting at which the vote is given`
        OR (`the vote is given on a poll taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded` AND `the company receives notice of the termination before the time appointed for taking the poll`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the validity of a vote given by that person unless the company receives notice of the termination— (a) before the commencement of the meeting or adjourned meeting at which the vote is given, or (b) in the case of a poll taken more than 48 hours after it is demanded, before the time appointed for taking the poll" -- FORK F8
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4206 | (4) If the company's articles require or permit members to give notice of termination to a person other than the company, the references above to the company receiving notice have effect as if they were or (as the case may be) included a reference to that person.
@ref s 330(4) Notice required of termination of proxy's authority: notice to another person (src:4206)
GIVEN `the company's articles require or permit members to give notice of termination to a person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of termination is received by that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(4) the company is treated as having received the notice` MEANS
    IF `the company's articles require or permit members to give notice of termination to a person other than the company` AND `the notice of termination is received by that person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the company's articles require or permit members to give notice of termination to a person other than the company" -- FORK F19

-- src:4207 | (5) Subsections (2) and (3) have effect subject to any provision of the company's articles which has the effect of requiring notice of termination to be received by the company or another person at a time earlier than that specified in those subsections.
-- src:4208 | This is subject to subsection (6).
@ref s 330(5) Notice required of termination of proxy's authority: an earlier time required by the articles (src:4207-4208)
GIVEN `the articles require notice of termination to be received at a time earlier than that specified in subsections (2) and (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is earlier than the time subsection (6) allows` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(5) the earlier time required by the articles has effect` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the articles require notice of termination to be received at a time earlier than that specified in subsections (2) and (3)`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any provision of the company's articles which has the effect of requiring notice of termination to be received by the company or another person at a time earlier than that specified in those subsections"
    ELSE IF `the requirement is earlier than the time subsection (6) allows`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is subject to subsection (6)" -- FORK F4
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 330(6) when the notice must be received` IS ONE OF
    `s 330(6)(a) in the case of a meeting or adjourned meeting, 48 hours before the time for holding it`
    `s 330(6)(b) in the case of a poll taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded, 24 hours before the time appointed for the taking of the poll`
    `s 330(6) another case`

-- src:4213 | (7) In calculating the periods mentioned in subsections (3)(b) and (6) no account shall be taken of any part of a day that is not a working day.
@ref s 330(7) Notice required of termination of proxy's authority: calculating the periods (src:4213)
GIVEN `hours in the period` IS A NUMBER
      `hours of the period that fall on a day that is not a working day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 330(7) the hours of the period that are counted` MEANS
    `hours in the period` MINUS `hours of the period that fall on a day that is not a working day`

-- src:4209 | (6) Any provision of the company's articles is void in so far as it would have the effect of requiring notice of termination to be received by the company or another person earlier than the following time—
-- src:4210 | (a) in the case of a meeting or adjourned meeting, 48 hours before the time for holding the meeting or adjourned meeting;
-- src:4211 | (b) in the case of a poll taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded, 24 hours before the time appointed for the taking of the poll;
-- src:4212 | (c) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 330(6) Notice required of termination of proxy's authority: the latest time the articles may require (src:4209-4212)
GIVEN case IS A `s 330(6) when the notice must be received`
      `hours before the relevant time that the articles require notice of termination to be received` IS A NUMBER
      `of those hours, the hours that fall on a day that is not a working day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(6) the provision of the articles is void` MEANS
    CONSIDER case
    WHEN `s 330(6) another case` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "earlier than the following time— (a) ... (b) ..."
    WHEN `s 330(6)(a) in the case of a meeting or adjourned meeting, 48 hours before the time for holding it` THEN
        IF `s 330(7) the hours of the period that are counted` `hours before the relevant time that the articles require notice of termination to be received` `of those hours, the hours that fall on a day that is not a working day` GREATER THAN 48
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is void in so far as it would have the effect of requiring notice of termination to be received by the company or another person earlier than the following time"
    WHEN `s 330(6)(b) in the case of a poll taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded, 24 hours before the time appointed for the taking of the poll` THEN
        IF `s 330(7) the hours of the period that are counted` `hours before the relevant time that the articles require notice of termination to be received` `of those hours, the hours that fall on a day that is not a working day` GREATER THAN 24
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is void in so far as it would have the effect of requiring notice of termination to be received by the company or another person earlier than the following time"

-- ---- s 331 Saving for more extensive rights conferred by articles -----------------------------------------

-- src:4215 | Nothing in sections 324 to 330 (proxies) prevents a company's articles from conferring more extensive rights on members or proxies than are conferred by those sections.
@ref s 331 Saving for more extensive rights conferred by articles (src:4215)
GIVEN `the articles confer more extensive rights on members or proxies than are conferred by sections 324 to 330` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 331 sections 324 to 330 prevent the articles from conferring the rights` MEANS
    IF `the articles confer more extensive rights on members or proxies than are conferred by sections 324 to 330`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in sections 324 to 330 (proxies) prevents a company's articles from conferring more extensive rights on members or proxies than are conferred by those sections"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "conferring more extensive rights"

§§ `Adjourned meetings`

-- ---- s 332 Resolution passed at adjourned meeting --------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4218 | Where a resolution is passed at an adjourned meeting of a company, the resolution is for all purposes to be treated as having been passed on the date on which it was in fact passed, and is not to be deemed passed on any earlier date.
@ref s 332 Resolution passed at adjourned meeting (src:4218)
GIVEN `the resolution is passed at an adjourned meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the resolution was in fact passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 332 the date on which the resolution is treated as having been passed` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is passed at an adjourned meeting of the company`
    THEN JUST `the date on which the resolution was in fact passed`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a resolution is passed at an adjourned meeting of a company"

§§ `Electronic communications`

-- ---- s 333 Sending documents relating to meetings etc in electronic form ---------------------------------

-- src:4221 | (1) Where a company has given an electronic address in a notice calling a meeting, it is deemed to have agreed that any document or information relating to proceedings at the meeting may be sent by electronic means to that address (subject to any conditions or limitations specified in the notice).
@ref s 333(1) Sending documents relating to meetings etc in electronic form (src:4221)
GIVEN `the company has given an electronic address in a notice calling a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or information relates to proceedings at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sending is within any conditions or limitations specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333(1) the company is deemed to have agreed that the document or information may be sent by electronic means to the address` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company has given an electronic address in a notice calling a meeting`) OR (NOT `the document or information relates to proceedings at the meeting`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company has given an electronic address in a notice calling a meeting, it is deemed to have agreed that any document or information relating to proceedings at the meeting may be sent by electronic means to that address" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `the sending is within any conditions or limitations specified in the notice`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(subject to any conditions or limitations specified in the notice)"

-- src:4222 | (2) Where a company has given an electronic address—
-- src:4223 | (a) in an instrument of proxy sent out by the company in relation to the meeting, or
-- src:4224 | (b) in an invitation to appoint a proxy issued by the company in relation to the meeting,
-- src:4225 | it is deemed to have agreed that any document or information relating to proxies for that meeting may be sent by electronic means to that address (subject to any conditions or limitations specified in the notice).
@ref s 333(2) Sending documents relating to meetings etc in electronic form: proxies (src:4222-4225)
GIVEN `the company has given an electronic address in an instrument of proxy sent out by the company in relation to the meeting, or in an invitation to appoint a proxy issued by the company in relation to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or information relates to proxies for that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sending is within any conditions or limitations specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333(2) the company is deemed to have agreed that the document or information relating to proxies may be sent by electronic means to the address` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company has given an electronic address in an instrument of proxy sent out by the company in relation to the meeting, or in an invitation to appoint a proxy issued by the company in relation to the meeting`)
        OR (NOT `the document or information relates to proxies for that meeting`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company has given an electronic address— (a) in an instrument of proxy sent out by the company in relation to the meeting, or (b) in an invitation to appoint a proxy issued by the company in relation to the meeting, it is deemed to have agreed" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `the sending is within any conditions or limitations specified in the notice`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(subject to any conditions or limitations specified in the notice)"

DECLARE `s 333(3) document` IS ONE OF
    `s 333(3)(a) the appointment of a proxy in relation to a meeting`
    `s 333(3)(b) any document necessary to show the validity of, or otherwise relating to, the appointment of a proxy`
    `s 333(3)(c) notice of the termination of the authority of a proxy`
    `s 333(3) another document`

-- src:4226 | (3) In subsection (2), documents relating to proxies include—
-- src:4227 | (a) the appointment of a proxy in relation to a meeting,
-- src:4228 | (b) any document necessary to show the validity of, or otherwise relating to, the appointment of a proxy, and
-- src:4229 | (c) notice of the termination of the authority of a proxy.
@ref s 333(3) Sending documents relating to meetings etc in electronic form: documents relating to proxies (src:4226-4229)
GIVEN document IS A `s 333(3) document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333(3) the document is a document relating to proxies` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `s 333(3) another document` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "documents relating to proxies include"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:4230 | (4) In this section “electronic address” means any address or number used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means.
@ref s 333(4) Sending documents relating to meetings etc in electronic form: "electronic address" (src:4230)
GIVEN `the address or number is used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333(4) the address or number is an electronic address` MEANS
    IF `the address or number is used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“electronic address” means any address or number used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means"

-- ---- s 333A Traded company: duty to provide electronic address for receipt of proxies etc ------------------

-- src:4232 | (1) A traded company must provide an electronic address for the receipt of any document or information relating to proxies for a general meeting.
@ref s 333A(1) Traded company: duty to provide electronic address for receipt of proxies etc (src:4232)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has provided an electronic address for the receipt of any document or information relating to proxies for the general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333A(1) the traded company has provided an electronic address` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A traded company must provide an electronic address"
    ELSE IF `the company has provided an electronic address for the receipt of any document or information relating to proxies for the general meeting`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A traded company must provide an electronic address for the receipt of any document or information relating to proxies for a general meeting" -- FORK F5

-- src:4233 | (2) The company must provide the address either—
-- src:4234 | (a) by giving it when sending out an instrument of proxy for the purposes of the meeting or issuing an invitation to appoint a proxy for those purposes; or
-- src:4235 | (b) by ensuring that it is made available, throughout the period beginning with the first date on which notice of the meeting is given and ending with the conclusion of the meeting, on the website on which the information required by section 311A(1) is made available.
@ref s 333A(2) Traded company: duty to provide electronic address for receipt of proxies etc: how (src:4233-4235)
GIVEN `the address was given when sending out an instrument of proxy for the purposes of the meeting or issuing an invitation to appoint a proxy for those purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address was made available, throughout the period beginning with the first date on which notice of the meeting was given and ending with the conclusion of the meeting, on the website on which the information required by section 311A(1) is made available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333A(2) the address was provided in a way this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the address was given when sending out an instrument of proxy for the purposes of the meeting or issuing an invitation to appoint a proxy for those purposes`
        OR `the address was made available, throughout the period beginning with the first date on which notice of the meeting was given and ending with the conclusion of the meeting, on the website on which the information required by section 311A(1) is made available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must provide the address either— (a) by giving it when sending out an instrument of proxy ...; or (b) by ensuring that it is made available" -- FORK F5

-- src:4236 | (3) The company is deemed to have agreed that any document or information relating to proxies for the meeting may be sent by electronic means to the address provided (subject to any limitations specified by the company when providing the address).
@ref s 333A(3) Traded company: duty to provide electronic address for receipt of proxies etc: deemed agreement (src:4236)
GIVEN `the company has provided an electronic address under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or information relates to proxies for the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sending is within any limitations specified by the company when providing the address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333A(3) the company is deemed to have agreed that the document or information may be sent by electronic means to the address` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company has provided an electronic address under this section`) OR (NOT `the document or information relates to proxies for the meeting`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any document or information relating to proxies for the meeting may be sent by electronic means to the address provided"
    ELSE IF `the sending is within any limitations specified by the company when providing the address`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(subject to any limitations specified by the company when providing the address)"

DECLARE `s 333A(4)(a) document` IS ONE OF
    `s 333A(4)(a)(i) the appointment of a proxy for a meeting`
    `s 333A(4)(a)(ii) any document necessary to show the validity of, or otherwise relating to, the appointment of a proxy`
    `s 333A(4)(a)(iii) notice of the termination of the authority of a proxy`
