§§ `Application to class meetings`

-- ---- s 334 Application to class meetings -----------------------------------------------------------------

-- The provisions of this Chapter are named by the text's own strings (a section, or a section and subsection).
-- src:4247 | (2) The following provisions of this Chapter do not apply in relation to a meeting of holders of a class of shares—
-- src:4248 | (a) sections 303 to 305 (members' power to require directors to call general meeting), . . .
-- src:4249 | (b) section 306 (power of court to order meeting), and
-- src:4250 | (c) sections 311(3), 311A, 319A, 327(A1), 330(A1) and 333A (additional requirements relating to traded companies).
@ref s 334(2) Application to class meetings: provisions that do not apply (src:4247-4250)
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 334(2) the provision of this Chapter does not apply in relation to a meeting of holders of a class of shares` MEANS
    IF elem provision (LIST "303", "304", "305", "306", "311(3)", "311A", "319A", "327(A1)", "330(A1)", "333A")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following provisions of this Chapter do not apply" does not say "only"

-- src:4251 | (2A) Section 307(1) to (6) apply in relation to a meeting of holders of a class of shares in a traded company as they apply in relation to a meeting of holders of a class of shares in a company other than a traded company (and, accordingly, section 307A does not apply in relation to such a meeting).
@ref s 334(2A) Application to class meetings: section 307 for traded companies (src:4251)
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 334(2A) the provision applies to a meeting of holders of a class of shares in a traded company` MEANS
    IF provision EQUALS "307(1) to (6)"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF provision EQUALS "307A"
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(and, accordingly, section 307A does not apply in relation to such a meeting)"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 307(1) to (6) apply in relation to a meeting of holders of a class of shares in a traded company" -- FORK F19

-- src:4252 | (3) The following provisions (in addition to those mentioned in subsection (2)) do not apply in relation to a meeting in connection with the variation of rights attached to a class of shares (a “variation of class rights meeting”)—
-- src:4253 | (a) section 318 (quorum), and
-- src:4254 | (b) section 321 (right to demand a poll).
@ref s 334(3) Application to class meetings: variation of class rights meetings (src:4252-4254)
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
      `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 334(3) the provision does not apply in relation to the variation of class rights meeting` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` AND elem provision (LIST "318", "321")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "do not apply in relation to a meeting in connection with the variation of rights attached to a class of shares"

-- src:4245 | (1) The provisions of this Chapter apply (with necessary modifications) in relation to a meeting of holders of a class of shares as they apply in relation to a general meeting.
-- src:4246 | This is subject to subsections (2) to (3).
@ref s 334(1) Application to class meetings (src:4245-4246)
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
      `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 334(1) the provision of this Chapter applies (with necessary modifications) to a meeting of holders of a class of shares` MEANS
    IF `s 334(2) the provision of this Chapter does not apply in relation to a meeting of holders of a class of shares` provision EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is subject to subsections (2) to (3)" -- FORK F4
    ELSE IF `s 334(3) the provision does not apply in relation to the variation of class rights meeting` provision `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is subject to subsections (2) to (3)" -- FORK F4
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4255 | (4) The quorum for a variation of class rights meeting is—
-- src:4256 | (a) for a meeting other than an adjourned meeting, two persons present holding at least one-third in nominal value of the issued shares of the class in question (excluding any shares of that class held as treasury shares);
-- src:4257 | (b) for an adjourned meeting, one person present holding shares of the class in question.
@ref s 334(4) Application to class meetings: quorum for a variation of class rights meeting (src:4255-4257)
GIVEN `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `persons present holding shares of the class in question` IS A NUMBER
      `nominal value of the issued shares of the class held by the persons present` IS A NUMBER
      `nominal value of the issued shares of the class in question (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 334(4) the quorum for the variation of class rights meeting is present` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The quorum for a variation of class rights meeting is"
    ELSE IF `the meeting is an adjourned meeting`
         THEN IF `persons present holding shares of the class in question` AT LEAST 1
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) for an adjourned meeting, one person present holding shares of the class in question"
         ELSE IF `persons present holding shares of the class in question` AT LEAST 2
                 AND `nominal value of the issued shares of the class held by the persons present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `nominal value of the issued shares of the class in question (excluding treasury shares)`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) for a meeting other than an adjourned meeting, two persons present holding at least one-third in nominal value of the issued shares of the class in question (excluding any shares of that class held as treasury shares)" -- FORK F19

-- src:4258 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4), where a person is present by proxy or proxies, he is treated as holding only the shares in respect of which those proxies are authorised to exercise voting rights.
@ref s 334(5) Application to class meetings: a person present by proxy (src:4258)
GIVEN `the person is present by proxy or proxies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `nominal value of the shares in respect of which those proxies are authorised to exercise voting rights` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 334(5) the nominal value of the shares the person is treated as holding` MEANS
    IF `the person is present by proxy or proxies`
    THEN JUST `nominal value of the shares in respect of which those proxies are authorised to exercise voting rights`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where a person is present by proxy or proxies, he is treated as holding only the shares in respect of which those proxies are authorised to exercise voting rights"

-- src:4259 | (6) At a variation of class rights meeting, any holder of shares of the class in question present may demand a poll.
@ref s 334(6) Application to class meetings: a poll (src:4259)
GIVEN `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a holder of shares of the class in question present at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 334(6) the holder may demand a poll` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` AND `the person is a holder of shares of the class in question present at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At a variation of class rights meeting, any holder of shares of the class in question present may demand a poll"

DECLARE `s 334(7) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 334(7)(a) any amendment of a provision contained in a company's articles for the variation of the rights attached to a class of shares, or the insertion of any such provision into the articles`
    `s 334(7)(b) the abrogation of rights attached to a class of shares`
