    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following provisions of this Chapter do not apply" does not say "only"

-- src:4269 | (3) The following provisions (in addition to those mentioned in subsection (2)) do not apply in relation to a meeting in connection with the variation of the rights of a class of members (a “variation of class rights meeting”)—
-- src:4270 | (a) section 318 (quorum), and
-- src:4271 | (b) section 321 (right to demand a poll).
@ref s 335(3) Application to class meetings: companies without a share capital: variation of class rights meetings (src:4269-4271)
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
      `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 335(3) the provision does not apply in relation to the variation of class rights meeting` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` AND elem provision (LIST "318", "321")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "do not apply in relation to a meeting in connection with the variation of the rights of a class of members"

-- src:4264 | (1) The provisions of this Chapter apply (with necessary modifications) in relation to a meeting of a class of members of a company without a share capital as they apply in relation to a general meeting.
-- src:4265 | This is subject to subsections (2) and (3).
@ref s 335(1) Application to class meetings: companies without a share capital (src:4264-4265)
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
      `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 335(1) the provision of this Chapter applies (with necessary modifications) to a meeting of a class of members` MEANS
    IF `s 335(2) the provision of this Chapter does not apply in relation to a meeting of a class of members` provision EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is subject to subsections (2) and (3)" -- FORK F4
    ELSE IF `s 335(3) the provision does not apply in relation to the variation of class rights meeting` provision `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is subject to subsections (2) and (3)" -- FORK F4
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4272 | (4) The quorum for a variation of class rights meeting is—
-- src:4273 | (a) for a meeting other than an adjourned meeting, two members of the class present (in person or by proxy) who together represent at least one-third of the voting rights of the class;
-- src:4274 | (b) for an adjourned meeting, one member of the class present (in person or by proxy).
@ref s 335(4) Application to class meetings: companies without a share capital: quorum (src:4272-4274)
GIVEN `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `members of the class present (in person or by proxy)` IS A NUMBER
      `voting rights of the class represented by the members of the class present` IS A NUMBER
      `total voting rights of the class` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 335(4) the quorum for the variation of class rights meeting is present` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The quorum for a variation of class rights meeting is"
    ELSE IF `the meeting is an adjourned meeting`
         THEN IF `members of the class present (in person or by proxy)` AT LEAST 1
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) for an adjourned meeting, one member of the class present (in person or by proxy)"
         ELSE IF `members of the class present (in person or by proxy)` AT LEAST 2
                 AND `voting rights of the class represented by the members of the class present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `total voting rights of the class`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) for a meeting other than an adjourned meeting, two members of the class present (in person or by proxy) who together represent at least one-third of the voting rights of the class" -- FORK F19

-- src:4275 | (5) At a variation of class rights meeting, any member present (in person or by proxy) may demand a poll.
@ref s 335(5) Application to class meetings: companies without a share capital: a poll (src:4275)
GIVEN `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member present (in person or by proxy) at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 335(5) the member may demand a poll` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` AND `the person is a member present (in person or by proxy) at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At a variation of class rights meeting, any member present (in person or by proxy) may demand a poll"

DECLARE `s 335(6) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 335(6)(a) any amendment of a provision contained in a company's articles for the variation of the rights of a class of members, or the insertion of any such provision into the articles`
    `s 335(6)(b) the abrogation of the rights of a class of members`
    `s 335(6) another act`

-- src:4276 | (6) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:4277 | (a) any amendment of a provision contained in a company's articles for the variation of the rights of a class of members, or the insertion of any such provision into the articles, is itself to be treated as a variation of those rights, and
-- src:4278 | (b) references to the variation of rights of a class of members include references to their abrogation.
@ref s 335(6) Application to class meetings: companies without a share capital: what is a variation (src:4276-4278)
GIVEN act IS A `s 335(6) act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 335(6) the act is treated as a variation of the rights of a class of members` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 335(6) another act` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to the variation of rights of a class of members include references to their abrogation"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
